    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nMount Alexander is a most attractive double fronted detached period-style residence, ideally positioned on St Mary's Road, one of Ballsbridge's most established and highly regarded tree-lined residential roads.\n\nBuilt in 1991, the property was designed in a traditional Victorian style, with high ceilings, decorative cornices and period-style fireplaces providing architectural character throughout. While it has the appearance and presence of an older Dublin residence, it offers the practical proportions, comfort and ease of maintenance associated with a more modern home. Importantly, Mount Alexander is not a protected structure.\n\nThe well-maintained accommodation provides generous and versatile living space, making the property suitable for a range of purchasers, including families, professional households and those seeking to downsize without moving to apartment living. The home offers ample space for entertaining and accommodating family and friends, while the manageable outdoor space reduces the maintenance often associated with a substantial detached residence.\n\nA particularly valuable feature is the private off-street parking for up to three cars, a rare amenity in such a central Dublin location. To the rear, a private patio garden provides a pleasant outdoor area suitable for al fresco dining, morning coffee or general relaxation.\n\nThe location is exceptional. St Mary's Road is within easy walking distance of Baggot Street, Ballsbridge village and a wide selection of restaurants, cafés, hotels and local amenities. Herbert Park and the Bishop's Garden are both nearby, providing attractive green spaces close to home. The Grand Canal, Sandymount, the city centre and Dublin's principal business districts are also readily accessible.\n\nThe area is particularly well served for education, with several leading primary and secondary schools within easy reach. UCD and Trinity College Dublin are also readily accessible, while the surrounding area offers a broad choice of sporting and recreational facilities, including golf and tennis clubs, gyms and parks.\n\nFor families, the property provides a well-connected base close to schools, universities, sport and the city centre. For professional purchasers, it combines a peaceful residential setting with convenient access to Dublin's commercial, cultural and social amenities. For those looking to simplify their lifestyle, it offers the opportunity to retain the space, privacy and character of a detached home without the upkeep of a large garden.\n\nMount Alexander represents a rare opportunity to acquire a detached period-style residence in one of Dublin 4's most desirable locations, combining traditional architectural character with modern practicality, generous parking and an excellent Ballsbridge address.\n\nSpecial Features\n\n- Substantial detached period-style residence.\n- Built in 1991.\n- Traditional Victorian-style design.\n- High ceilings, decorative coving and period-style fireplaces.\n- Stained wooden floors on the ground floor, carpeted except for the Dining Room.\n- Well-maintained and versatile accommodation.\n- Private off-street parking for up to 3 cars.\n- Private rear patio garden.\n- Situated on one of Ballsbridge's established tree-lined residential roads.\n- Within easy walking distance of Baggot Street, local restaurants, cafés and hotels.\n- Close to Herbert Park and the Bishop's Garden.\n- Convenient access to schools, universities, sporting facilities and Dublin city centre.\n- Not a protected structure."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway: - \nbeautiful stained-glass fanlight, welcoming and spacious hallway with high ceiling, ornate coving and centre rose.\n\nLiving Room: - \nelegant reception room with cast iron fireplace and coal effect gas fire and sash windows.\n\nSunroom: - \nwith attractive panelled ceiling and walls, superb bright and comfortable room.\n\nDining Room: - \nwith cast iron fireplace with coal effect gas fire, stained wooden floor. High ceiling with ornate coving and centre rose sash window.\n\nKitchen/Breakfast Room: - \nwith a superb range of built in wall and floor units, integrated oven, hob, extractor fan, dishwasher and fridge freezer, granite worktops, attractive tiled splashback, panelled ceiling with recessed lighting. Door to the patio garden.\n\nGuest w.c.: - \nw.c. and wash hand basin.\n\nUPSTAIRS - \n\n\nUpstairs: - \nattractive arched stained-glass window.\n\nLanding: - \nbright and spacious landing with attractive coving and centre rose. Hotpress with good storage.\n\nMain Bedroom: - \nsuperb spacious double bedroom with an excellent range of built in wardrobes and shelving. Ceiling coving, centre rose and sash window.\n\nEnsuite Shower Room: - \nwith large shower cubicle, w.c. and wash hand basin. Part panelled walls, ceiling coving and built in shelving.\n\nBedroom 2: - \nsuperb double room with built in wardrobes, sash window and overlooking the front garden.\n\nBedroom 3: - \ndouble room with built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 4 / Study: - \nattractive arched sash windows. Built in display unit with underneath units. Stira access to the spacious attic.\n\nFamily Bathroom: - \nbath and shower, w.c, bidet and wash hand basin, part panelled walls and built in shelving.\n\nLarge Attic: - \nfully floored with lighting suitable for storage.\n\nUtility Room (outside): - \nplumbed for washing machine. Excellent storage and built in shelving.\n\n"
      },
